{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/620110-sourcebooks-that-should-not-be-read","id":620110,"title":"Sourcebooks that should not be read?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T09:13:23-07:00","id":620110,"title":"Sourcebooks that should not be read?","content":"Greetings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I heard a lot of good stuff about most of the sourcebooks for WTO, but are there any that are better left in a closet? I'm thinking about stuff like 'Chaos Factor' here.<br /> <br /> I only ask this question because I'm thinking about buying the bundle on drivethrpg. And another question about the bundle itself: How good is the quality of the scanned books? I remember buying Veil of Night a few years ago and not being overly impressed (the new-and-improved original electronic one is great though.)<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7182-curiel","name":"Curiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:26:51-07:00","id":620159,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of the Guildbooks add anything. They overstate what their influence should be. I wouldn't say they were abysmal though, just useless. A single volume covering all the Guides would have congealed the few gold flakes and gotten rid of the padding.<br /> <br /> Wraith has one of the stronger set of sourcebooks. I think all you need is Spectres, Sea of Shadows, Doomslayers, Shadow Player's Guide, and Wraith Player's Guide. Hierarchy and Renegades are also good, but not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:07:29-07:00","id":620217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/620110-sourcebooks-that-should-not-be-read?p=620159#post620159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any of the Guildbooks add anything. They overstate what their influence should be. I wouldn't say they were abysmal though, just useless. A single volume covering all the Guides would have congealed the few gold flakes and gotten rid of the padding.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Mm. I'd question the 'not adding anything' for a number of Guilds, not least the Spooks, who went from being random delinquents and thugs in the corebooks to being Stygia's mafia/yakuza in their splatbook, and the Mnemoi in their mini-Guildbook in Ends of Empire.<br /> <br /> (And I have kind of a nostalgic fondness for the Sandman Guildbook.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T10:29:02-07:00","id":620238,"title":"","content":"I've never played Wraith but I have a soft spot in my heart for <i>The Risen</i> (what can I say, I'm a big James O'Barr's The Crow fan) and for <i>Love Beyond Death</i>. I couldn't call them must-haves, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T12:44:44-07:00","id":620397,"title":"","content":"I don't own any of the Guild books, so I cannot say with conviction anything other than what little I could glean from thumbing through them at <b>Black and Read</b>... As for the rest, even the ones I didn't love like <i>Book of Legions</i>* and especially <i>Mediums: Speakers with the Dead</i> had some BRILLIANT stuff in them.<br /> <br /> * And IF you want the whole rundown of what I didn't love about <i>Book of Legions</i> I can give it, but honestly? At the moment I cannot remember all them... Besides, all of my books are packed away pending a restoration project in my 'lair' so I cannot consult it at the moment anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T01:54:20-07:00","id":621002,"title":"","content":"I don't think WtO had any really flat out bad supplements. There's certainly a range, but mostly from &quot;meh&quot; to &quot;awesome.&quot; It managed to avoid the, &quot;holy shit stay away,&quot; books fairly solidly.<br /> <br /> Almost any book I can think of with WtO content that I'd avoid are going to be the WOD crossover style books.<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses of Europe probably deserves a side note in this. It's a good book, but the subject matter is harsh; even by WtO standards. It most certainly isn't a, &quot;should not read,&quot; in the sense of the more notoriously bad cWOD books, but there are people I would not hand it to because I know they wouldn't be able to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:46:11-07:00","id":621249,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Nothing in the WtO line was horrible. Even the \u2018meh\u2019 books have something you can take away. I never bothered with any of the Guildbooks but I\u2019ve heard from other forumites that they add a great deal of depth (marin mentioned the details of the Spooks and \u2013 a while ago \u2013 I think Possessed talked about the depth that the Haunter Guildbook added).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">And because it\u2019s precisely what you didn\u2019t ask for, here is a list of [what I think are] must-reads for WtO.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Must-Reads, in no particular order:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"><i>Doomslayers</i> \u2013 Some good stuff on Spectres, the Labyrinth, and insight into professional subcultures that exist on the fringe of proper Stygian society.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"><i>Shadow Players Guide</i> \u2013 That\u2019s half your character!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"><i>Book of Legions</i> \u2013 I love this book. I love the setting-fiction between chapters and the fluff. The crunch is \u2018meh\u2019, but that was never really my thing. This book felt like what Hierarchy should have been, although BoL focuses on the military aspects of the Legions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"><i>Dark Reflections</i> \u2013 \u2018Cuz I still believe the best way to create your Shadow is to think about what kind of spectre (not necessarily Caste) your character would be.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"><i>Charnel Houses</i> is an absolutely wonderful book! It\u2019s harsh, it\u2019s horrible, it\u2019s true, and not for everyone, but I really appreciate what it accomplished. IIRC, It reads like a history book* with WtO material presented as sidebars. I know it has critics, but I think (especially with the information prefaced in the introduction) it was respectfully done.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">*I aced a history test in high school solely because of CHoE.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:37:10-07:00","id":621448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/620110-sourcebooks-that-should-not-be-read?p=621002#post621002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think WtO had any really flat out bad supplements. There's certainly a range, but mostly from &quot;meh&quot; to &quot;awesome.&quot; It managed to avoid the, &quot;holy shit stay away,&quot; books fairly solidly.<br /> <br /> Almost any book I can think of with WtO content that I'd avoid are going to be the WOD crossover style books.<br /> <br /> Charnel Houses of Europe probably deserves a side note in this. It's a good book, but the subject matter is harsh; even by WtO standards. It most certainly isn't a, &quot;should not read,&quot; in the sense of the more notoriously bad cWOD books, but there are people I would not hand it to because I know they wouldn't be able to read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there really isn't any offensively bad WtO books. There are bland and uninteresting books but that's really about the worst it has. There are books I'd say are 'read only if it interests you', but beyond that aren't any I'd say to avoid altogether.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair with some of the horrible WoD books they have a 'so bad its good' quality to them and I'd recommend reading once if you ever got the chance because of God-awful and/or silly they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:56:47-07:00","id":621455,"title":"","content":"Thanks for helping me out here guys, I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> @Charnel Houses of Europe: Considering the topic of that particular sourcebook, I'm not really surprised that its dark(er).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7182-curiel","name":"Curiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T20:29:11-07:00","id":621852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/620110-sourcebooks-that-should-not-be-read?p=620217#post620217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Mm. I'd question the 'not adding anything' for a number of Guilds, not least the Spooks, who went from being random delinquents and thugs in the corebooks to being Stygia's mafia/yakuza in their splatbook, and the Mnemoi in their mini-Guildbook in Ends of Empire.<br /> <br /> (And I have kind of a nostalgic fondness for the Sandman Guildbook.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah - I was going to reply that post with &quot;Spoken like a true hierarchy fan!&quot;. The guilds are what made Wraith, in my opinion and those of the groups that I was storyteller for. Most games from far future to near bronze age have the &quot;empire&quot; and the &quot;rebels&quot; - with Wraith having the Hierarchy and the Renegades and Heretics. Very few have these hard to describe, very different, 13 entities that exist in varying levels of legality but without which the Hierarchy would collapse anyways (and yes, the Hierarchy would be just another small minor kingdom without the symbiotic relationship with the guilds I feel).<br /> <br /> As my friend above pointed out, the Spooks handbook is a prime example of a must read. Probably the best guidlbook out there in terms of &quot;you thought they thugs&quot;, but they're actually &quot;passionate mafia/yakuza with the core Cause of trying to watch out for your fellow wraith and save them from Oblivion&quot;.<br /> <br /> God I miss that book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:49:21-07:00","id":622689,"title":"","content":"<i>World of Darkness: Tokyo</i> is eminently skippable. I've only read it the once, and while I don't recall it necessarily being <u>bad</u>, I didn't care for it. It was part of White Wolf's &quot;Year of the Lotus&quot; push in 1998 when Kindred of the East debuted. <i>Mediums: Speakers with the Dead </i>&amp; <i>The Quick and the Dead</i> were pretty forgettable, at least for me, since they never really saw much use at the table. <i>The Face of Death</i> is good for putting yourself in a mood, but it's really just an art book.<br /> <br /> Overall, the quality of books for <i>Wraith </i>were above-standard, probably by dint of it being dead-last in sales (pun intended). Even <i>Changeling </i>was booted over to the Arthaus imprint instead of being canceled. <i>Wraith </i>never really suffered from the bloat and power-creep like the bigger game lines, and with comparatively smaller and fewer releases, more time and care could be spent on development.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:37:52-07:00","id":637568,"title":"","content":"From what I remember, Doomslayers, Spectres, and players guide to the shadow were awesome books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:39:39-07:00","id":637569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Curiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/620110-sourcebooks-that-should-not-be-read?p=621455#post621455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for helping me out here guys, I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> @Charnel Houses of Europe: Considering the topic of that particular sourcebook, I'm not really surprised that its dark(er).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, Charnel houses of Europe was extremely good too, just be prepared for what is inside, pretty dark stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:38:29-07:00","id":655104,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure on anything I'd advise steering clear o